| :---: | :---  |
| 0     | [10] -> [15] -> [20] |
| 1 | — |
| 2 | [12] |
| 3 | — |
| 4 | — |
How it works: All keys that hash to the same index are stored in a linked list.

- in index of 0 have 3 values , so every values have key:value.
using hash(value)-> key generated.
eg. If you store 10 use:- hash(10)

-So this procss called Chaining technique.

